{"availability":"available","full":"mattn/tensai","name":"tensai","description":"A tiny neural-network framework in pure Go with AVX2 SIMD kernels (GOEXPERIMENT=simd)","category":"Education","language":"Go","stars":112,"forks":6,"created":"2026-08-19T09:06:30Z","updated":"2026-10-07T17:05:22Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mattn.github.io/tensai/","topics":["autograd","avx2","deep-learning","gguf","golang","llm","machine-learning","neural-networks","onnx","quantization","safetensors","simd","tflite","tokenizer","webgpu"],"demo":"https://mattn.github.io/tensai/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.836Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.836Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.836Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.836Z","stars":112,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["tensai is a small machine-learning framework for learning and experiments. It implements forward passes, backpropagation, and optimization in pure Go; the default build has no external dependencies (the optional wgpu build tag adds exactly one, cgo-free: ebitengine/purego).","Documentation: mattn.github.io/tensai — guides for every package, in English and 日本語."],"features":["Matrix operations - Matrix plus basic operations such as Dot, Add, T, and AddBias. Tensors are float32 (tensai.Float)","N-dimensional tensors - Tensor generalizes Matrix to any rank: element-wise Add/Sub/Mul/Div with NumPy-style broadcasting, batched MatMul (the leading axes broadcast, the per-matrix products run on the same kernel as…","SIMD acceleration - AVX2 kernels on amd64 and NEON (ARM's Advanced SIMD) kernels on arm64, written with Go's experimental simd/archsimd package: still pure Go, no cgo, no assembly files. Matmul, ReLU/LeakyReLU,…","Low-allocation training - layers reuse their forward/backward scratch buffers across training steps (a full MLP step runs in 29 allocations), so GC stays out of the training loop; Predict always returns freshly…","Layers - Embedding, Dense, Conv2D, MaxPool2D, BatchNorm, LayerNorm, Dropout, plus ReLU, LeakyReLU, GELU, Sigmoid, Tanh, and Softmax activations"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mattn/tensai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b2703a529ede7923ddb05affc96bbf22ad5b07322f9f68df3afef509cbf14c43","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.990Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.990Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"tensai is a small machine-learning framework for learning and experiments. It implements forward passes, backpropagation, and optimization in pure Go; the default build has no external dependencies (the optional wgpu build tag adds exactly one, cgo-free: ebitengine/purego).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mattn/tensai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b2703a529ede7923ddb05affc96bbf22ad5b07322f9f68df3afef509cbf14c43","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mattn/tensai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.991Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T17:05:22Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mattn/tensai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:42.993Z","hash":"b2703a529ede7923ddb05affc96bbf22ad5b07322f9f68df3afef509cbf14c43","originalBytes":48059,"storedBytes":48059,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["example","model","run","tensai","same","wgpu","gpu","kernels","matmul","through","cpu","every","simd","which","one","weights","attention","runs","build","avx2","softmax","tags","tensor","mnist","step","autograd","token","windows","batch","each","load","training","against","back","backward","dense","dot","encoding","gguf","goexperiment","matrix","resident","vulkan","wgpu24","float32","only","per","tflite","tok","where","batched","kernel","models","out","path","tensors","whole","api","arm64","block","both","decode","gpt-2","graph","inputs","int8","layer","layers","lib","llama.cpp","nothing","plus","weight